.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:82:For non-native CLI executors, the workflow owns executor provenance. It writes a pre-dispatch sentinel, then patches the first canonical `"type":"iteration"` record with the `executor` block before `post_dispatch_validate` runs. Do NOT append your own `dispatch_failure` event or a partial fallback record when the executor itself crashes or times out; the workflow emits the typed failure event on that path.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.1.0.md:17:- **Review packets move to `review/`.** The review-mode contract moves the canonical review output paths from `scratch/` to `review/`. The automatic review workflow gains `review/` packet creation, migration and a resume flow, and the confirm workflow matches that contract.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.1.0.md:18:- **The review taxonomy is simplified.** The automatic review workflow and the `deep-review` agent use the simplified taxonomy, and the agent follows the `review/` packet contract in every runtime mirror.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/resume-classification-from-valid-prior-state.md:3:description: "Verify that the workflow classifies an existing valid scratch state as resumable before writing new files."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/resume-classification-from-valid-prior-state.md:15:This scenario validates resume classification from valid prior state for `DR-005`. The objective is to verify that the workflow classifies an existing valid scratch state as resumable before writing new files.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/resume-classification-from-valid-prior-state.md:27:- Objective: Verify that the workflow classifies an existing valid scratch state as resumable before writing new files.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/resume-classification-from-valid-prior-state.md:28:- Real user request: I already have a deep-research scratch folder. Tell me whether the workflow will resume it or start over.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/resume-classification-from-valid-prior-state.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.8.0.0.md:13:Research iterations can now run through `codex exec` with a chosen model, reasoning effort and service tier instead of relying only on the native research agent with Claude Opus. The YAML workflow continues to own state tracking, convergence detection, lifecycle events and the reducer. The CLI runs inside that workflow, not as a replacement, and this release ships as a symmetric pair with `deep-review` v1.5.0.0.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/quick-reference.md:38:- convergence stop contract: `references/convergence/convergence.md`, `references/convergence/convergence-signals.md`, and the deep-research YAML workflow
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/quick-reference.md:78:/deep:research  -->  YAML workflow  -->  @deep-research agent (LEAF)
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/quick-reference.md:170:6. Let the workflow reducer update `deep-research-strategy.md`, `findings-registry.json`, and `deep-research-dashboard.md`
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/research-charter-validation.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:3:description: "A finished fan-out research run now closes as complete, both research workflows honor --stop-policy=max-iterations and confirm mode has its quality guards back."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:14:A fan-out research run (one research topic split across several models, each running its own lineage) now closes as complete once its synthesis is written. Both research workflows also run to their ceiling when asked, and confirm mode checks quality again before it stops.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:23:- **`--stop-policy=max-iterations` holds in both workflows.** Auto and confirm now run to their iteration ceiling when asked. The rule is its own step, so the default convergence mode cannot skip it.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:24:- **Confirm mode has its quality guards back.** An earlier edit that aligned the two workflows dropped the quality checks from confirm's convergence step, so it could stop without them. They are back, and a test now holds each confirm workflow to its auto twin.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.1.0.md:25:- **The close-out runs from one shared script.** Both research workflows call the deep-loop runtime's close-out script, which also matches a finding by its `findingId` field.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/state-management/rejected-pattern-cache.md:27:Candidate filtering checks exact normalized text first, then applies category-compatible fuzzy matching using `rejectedPatternFuzzyThreshold` when present. The auto workflow consults reducer-derived `rejectedPatterns`, `rejectedPatternIndex`, and `suppressedCandidates` before next-focus, recovery, or ideas-backed candidates are dispatched.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-format.md:102:| `auto-generated` | Reducer/workflow regenerates the full file |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-format.md:123:- Do not treat legacy aliases as write targets. The workflow reads legacy aliases only for migration windows and writes canonical `deep-research-*` names.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-format.md:137:`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs` scans the workflow assets and runtime scripts and fails (exit 2) when a registered stem has no producer, a spoken stem has no emitter, or a reserved stem is emitted anyway.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-format.md:145:The projection folds only registered stems, and its `run_initialized` arm rebuilds a thin config row: `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, `timestamp`. A pre-flip config row written by the workflow carries more — `convergenceThreshold`, `minIterations`, `minIdeaObservations`, `antiConvergence`, `sessionId`, `executor`, `specFolder`, `createdAt` — and a refresh cannot rebuild those keys.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-jsonl.md:353:When every candidate matches an active rejected pattern, the auto workflow halts for operator input. In a ledger-backed run, one with a `deep-research-ledger/frames` folder beside the state log, the next projection replaces a hand-edited state log, so record the removal or reset through the append gateway. Write the row to a file, then hand it over:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md:178:- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/invalid-or-contradictory-state-halts-for-repair.md:28:- Real user request: My deep-research scratch folder looks half-broken. Will the workflow repair it automatically or stop?
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/invalid-or-contradictory-state-halts-for-repair.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.2.0.md:13:This patch tightens the research reducer and surrounding reference docs so they describe the same behavior. It fixes state handling, restores visible run-history data and closes a few cases where the workflow could silently drift from the docs.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.2.0.md:24:- **Completed sessions are no longer re-entered for synthesis.** Both workflow YAMLs routed completed sessions straight to the synthesize step, although the expected behavior called that unsupported. A completed packet is now a hard stop that requires an explicit operator choice to restart, archive or exit.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:17:The goal is to make the workflow easier to follow and easier to trust.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:22:- **Canonical packet artifacts are aligned.** Skill docs, references, runtime mirrors and workflow assets carry the packet contract across those surfaces.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:43:Canonical `deep-research-*` packet artifacts are now frozen across the skill docs, references, runtime mirrors and workflow assets. `SKILL.md` freezes the lifecycle vocabulary, reducer ownership, lineage and runtime contract guidance, and the README reframes the skill around the canonical research-only packet model.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md:51:OpenCode, Claude, Codex and the compatibility wrapper now describe the same deep-research packet expected behavior. The auto and confirm workflow YAML assets carry the same lifecycle, migration, registry and reducer expectations. The manual testing playbook now describes reducer-owned refresh behavior consistently in the root playbook and concrete iteration scenarios.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md:92:- `noProgressThreshold`: implementation default aligned with the workflow's recovery check
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.7.0.md:23:- **A lineage's reducer now writes into the lineage folder.** `reduce-state.cjs` takes `--artifact-dir`. Both research workflows pass the lineage folder on every per-iteration call, so the lineage's registry, dashboard and strategy stay current.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.7.0.md:24:- **Single-executor runs keep their behavior.** The workflows pass the flag only when a fan-out lineage directory is present, so a run without one resolves its artifact root as before.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-outputs.md:94:`research.md` is the workflow-owned synthesis output at `{artifact_dir}/research.md`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-outputs.md:101:- generated or machine-owned sections must be marked explicitly when the workflow uses them;
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:18:- **A `:review` suffix selects review mode.** The `.opencode/commands/speckit/deep-research.md` command detects the suffix, asks review setup questions and routes to the review workflows.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:19:- **Review runs in an autonomous or an interactive workflow.** The autonomous workflow runs four phases with review convergence and `review-report.md` synthesis, and the interactive workflow adds five approval gates.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:22:- **`AGENTS.md` files register the new agent.** The Public and Barter `AGENTS.md` files and `AGENTS_example_fs_enterprises.md` add `@deep-review` and an `@speckit` exception, and the Public file also adds the review workflow.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:17:Operator contract precedence for this skill surface (highest first): command entrypoint syntax in `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`; convergence math in `references/convergence/convergence.md` and the deep-research YAML workflow; runtime agent inventories from the checked-in runtime directories above.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:88:The YAML workflow owns executor selection: native `@deep-research` by default, or a routed CLI executor. Never use ad hoc shell loops.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:140:`/deep:research` owns the YAML workflow: it initializes state, dispatches one LEAF iteration at a time, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `research/research.md`, and saves continuity. `@deep-research` executes only one research cycle per dispatch.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:161:The workflow then:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:190:9. **Treat research/research.md as workflow-owned** -- Iteration findings feed synthesis, and the workflow owns the canonical `research/research.md`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:195:13. **Respect reducer ownership** -- The workflow reducer, not the agent, is the source of truth for strategy machine-owned sections, dashboard metrics, and findings registry updates
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:197:15. **Invoke through the command workflow** -- Use `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`, and let the YAML workflow own dispatch
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md:17:Open this when a research loop stalls, throws a workflow error or hits state problems it cannot recover from on its own. The stop contract itself lives in `convergence.md`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md:33:Recovery must be visible in packet state. The workflow records pivots and failures instead of silently changing direction.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md:41:The workflow emits or records recovery state rather than silently changing focus. Recovery attempts should be visible in the JSONL event stream, strategy file, registry, and dashboard.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md:106:Recovery fails when it repeats prior sources/findings, produces no new evidence, and does not narrow the search space. After repeated recovery failure, the loop may stop with open gaps or escalate to the user, depending on the configured workflow mode.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md:117:| 4. Direct Mode Fallback | Executor or dispatch path fails repeatedly | Use the workflow-supported fallback path |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/state-management/question-conflict-ownership.md:27:The workflow surfaces those disagreements through `question_conflict` JSONL events. Supported operator decisions are `accepted`, `rejected`, `superseded`, and `needs_decision`; unresolved conflicts default to `needs_decision` so the loop does not silently choose a winner.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:34:The YAML workflow owns lifecycle orchestration, `@deep-research` executes LEAF iterations, and the reducer synchronizes packet state after each iteration and lifecycle transition.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:121:The runtime supports three lineage modes today. `fork` and `completed-continue` were described in earlier drafts but have no workflow wiring in this release, so they MUST NOT be exposed to operators. If the long-form lineage feature is picked up later it will arrive with first-class event emission, reducer ancestry handling, and replay fixtures; until then treat the contract below as canonical.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:215:If the legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, the workflow MUST append the `blocked_stop` JSONL event before continuing. Reducers and dashboards consume the persisted event; they must not infer blocked-stop state solely from prose logs.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:232:When every candidate is suppressed, the auto workflow halts for operator input. In a ledger-backed run the operator records the `idea_rejected_removed` or `idea_rejected_reset` row through the append gateway (`append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory <artifact dir> --event-json <row file>`), never by editing the state log, which the next projection replaces. The row shapes and the full command are in `../state/state-jsonl.md` section 7.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:278:- `cli-claude-code`: `claude -p "$(cat prompt)" --model X --permission-mode acceptEdits --output-format text` with optional `--effort Y`. Default permission-mode is `plan` (read-only); we override to `acceptEdits` so iteration writes succeed. The inline workflow branches are not the complete schema: `cli-codex` is also an inline branch, while `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-deepseek-harness` (experimental) use the shared fan-out adapters; the executor-kind authority is `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` (`EXECUTOR_KINDS`).
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:438:An optional parallel execution concept for research topics with multiple independent questions. Treat this as reference guidance only; the live workflow remains sequential and does **not** emit wave-specific JSONL events or routing today.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:542:Compile all iteration findings into final research/research.md. The synthesis workflow owns the canonical `research/research.md` output.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:580:2. **No extra indexing step in the live contract**: `generate-context.js` is the supported save boundary for this workflow
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:644:In confirm mode, the YAML workflow adds approval gates:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md:57:The shared convergence runtime accepts four values. The workflow keeps hard terminal boundaries outside mode-specific convergence handling.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md:68:Research pivots are eligible only when the workflow decision is `STOP` and the exact internal reason is `composite_converged` or `all_questions_answered`. The legal-stop and quality gates run before this branch. `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `minIterationsNotReached`, `error`, `manualStop`, and `userPaused` are explicitly excluded. Max iterations, pause or cancellation, manual stop, and unrecoverable error therefore never dispatch a pivot Council.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md:92:| `error` | The loop hit an unrecoverable workflow or state error |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md:139:Every non-terminal STOP candidate must pass the gate bundle before the workflow exits.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md:160:| `../state/state-jsonl.md` | Need JSONL event shapes persisted by the convergence workflow |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md:169:- Do not change the YAML workflow by editing this document. This document describes and routes the live contract; workflow changes require command/YAML work.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/fresh-initialization-creates-canonical-state-files.md:42:2. Follow the listed command sequence in order so higher-level docs are checked before lower-level workflow contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/fresh-initialization-creates-canonical-state-files.md:49:2. `bash: rg -n 'step_create_directories|step_create_config|step_create_state_log|step_create_strategy' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml`
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/fresh-initialization-creates-canonical-state-files.md:75:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` | Autonomous init steps; inspect `phase_init` |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/initialization-and-state-setup/fresh-initialization-creates-canonical-state-files.md:76:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` | Interactive init steps; inspect `phase_init` |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.15.10.0.md:27:- **The executor contract reads as steps.** What the workflow owns, what is discouraged, which file owns the executor kinds and which YAML branch covers which executor now each stand alone.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:3:description: "This release updates the deep-research workflow around validation coverage, adding quality guards, a generated dashboard, new iteration state fields and research-charter validation."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:13:This release updates the deep-research workflow around validation coverage, adding quality guards, a generated dashboard, new iteration state fields and research-charter validation. The command documentation updates its workflow overview, the agents on five runtimes gain the same v1.1.0 features and the manual testing playbook adds scenarios.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:17:- **Quality guards gate convergence.** `references/convergence.md` gains a Quality Guard Protocol, and `loop-protocol.md` adds a quality guard check at Step 2c. The auto workflow applies the guard in its convergence check, the confirm workflow adds a quality guard, the state format records `guard_violation` events, and `quick-reference.md` adds a quality guards note.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:18:- **A dashboard is generated after each iteration.** The new `assets/deep-research-dashboard.md` template has 8 numbered sections, retrieval anchors and an Overview with Purpose and Usage. `loop-protocol.md` adds dashboard generation at Step 4a, `state-format.md` adds the dashboard schema, both workflow YAMLs gain a `step_generate_dashboard` step, and the config adds the dashboard to `fileProtection`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:25:- **The skill and command docs describe the new features.** `SKILL.md` bumps the skill version from 1.0.0 to 1.1.0 and gains 3 new ALWAYS rules, a quality gates row, the iteration status enum and a dashboard reference, and the README adds the v1.1.0 features, a version history section and the dashboard in its structure tree. The `deep-research` command doc updates its workflow overview for the charter, guards and dashboard and expands its Key Differences. The confirm workflow gains a resume decision gate, and both workflow YAMLs gain a version comment.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-reference-only.md:33:Reference-only models cannot affect runtime STOP decisions unless the YAML workflow, reducer, and live convergence references are updated in the same packet.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-reference-only.md:41:The live workflow uses a single segment by default. Earlier designs allowed `state.iterations` to be filtered by an active segment before convergence. That remains reference-only.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-reference-only.md:75:These are not active workflow signals. Do not route implementation decisions through them unless the YAML workflow and reducer are updated in the same packet.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:15:On the live path, `deep_loop_graph_upsert` and `deep_loop_graph_convergence` run in the auto and confirm workflows. Reducer-owned surfaces expose `graphConvergenceScore`, `graphDecision` and `graphBlockers`, while blocked-stop JSONL events appear in the findings registry, dashboard and strategy `next-focus` anchor.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:19:The workflow is meant to be easier to follow and easier to trust.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:23:- **Blocked stops become recorded workflow events.** The `blocked_stop` event carries blocker and recovery context into reducers.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:38:Both research workflows emit a first-class `blocked_stop` JSONL event through `step_emit_blocked_stop`. Its `blockedBy`, `gateResults`, `recoveryStrategy` and full session run history give downstream reducers the exact blocker and recovery context.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:44:At emission, `step_normalize_pause_events` maps raw `paused` and `stuck_recovery` to `userPaused` and `stuckRecovery` using the frozen `STOP_REASONS` enum. The live workflow no longer passes free-form strings into `synthesis_complete.stopReason`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:50:In `deep_research_auto.yaml` and `deep_research_confirm.yaml`, `deep_loop_graph_upsert` runs after `step_reduce_state` and persists iteration `graphEvents` to the SQLite store. `deep_loop_graph_convergence` runs before the inline three-signal vote in `step_check_convergence`, and `STOP_BLOCKED` routes to `blocked_stop` emission. The OpenCode `deep-research` agent gains explicit graph tool permissions, and the Claude agent mirrors them.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:3:description: "Deep-research's graph work now has a peer skill of its own. The change gives its workflows a direct route to graph state instead of relying on a separate skill's MCP server."
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:13:Deep-research's graph work now has a peer skill of its own. The change gives its workflows a direct route to graph state instead of relying on a separate skill's MCP server.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:19:Before arc 118, workflow steps that needed graph state passed through an MCP marshalling layer. The arrangement had accumulated drift with no ADR to justify it.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:47:Before arc 118, `deep_research_auto.yaml` and `deep_research_confirm.yaml` dispatched graph operations through tools registered with the spec-memory MCP server. Both workflows now invoke scripts directly for convergence, upsert, query and status, following the pattern already used by `reduce-state.cjs`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md:65:The `deep-loop-runtime` v1.0.0 changelog is `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-runtime/changelog/v1.0.0.md`. The mirror release for `deep-review` v1.4.0.0 is `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-review/changelog/v1.4.0.0.md`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md:31:- **Generated by:** Orchestrator (step_generate_dashboard in YAML workflow)
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:39:This protocol does not own the shared intake contract in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md`, nor `/speckit:plan` or `/speckit:complete` delegation behavior.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:42:The workflow remains four-phase:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:57:- Ownership: acquired by the deep-research workflow, not by the leaf agent
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:77:- Release records whether the workflow ended with save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:103:- The workflow records a typed `spec_check_result` audit event before any mutation branch executes.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:142:The workflow writes or replaces exactly one machine-owned fence nested under the chosen host anchor:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:153:- The workflow replaces the full block atomically when content changes.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:159:- The workflow must not create duplicate generated blocks in sibling sections.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:167:Each spec-protocol row a workflow writes keeps its legacy shape. The append gateway accepts it and stores it as a typed ledger event under one of seven stems:
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md:208:- The shared intake contract (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md` §5-§6) applies the same normalization before writing `feature_description` into `spec.md` Problem Statement or Purpose; equivalent normalized phrases emit `intake_topic_deduped` instead of overwriting the existing prose.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/README.md:16:`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/` contains the code entrypoints used by the deep-research workflow. The modules cover divergent research pivots, state reduction and sparkline output, runtime capability reporting and YAML-backed script path checks.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/README.md:27:| `runtime-capabilities.cjs` | Reports runtime capabilities used by the research workflow. |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/README.md:28:| `verify-yaml-script-paths.sh` | Validates script paths referenced by YAML workflow assets. |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/state-management/jsonl-state-log.md:27:The log is append-only by contract. The agent may add one iteration line, the workflow may append event lines, and the reader path is fault-tolerant. Malformed lines are skipped with defaults instead of breaking the loop, and reconstruction from iteration files is an explicit recovery path when the log is damaged.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/state-management/jsonl-state-log.md:40:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` | Workflow | Appends workflow-owned events such as `graph_convergence` and `blocked_stop`. |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-graph.md:75:If graph data says `STOP_BLOCKED`, the workflow emits a blocked-stop path and continues.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.9.0.0.md:13:This release completes the executor expansion begun in v1.8.0.0 by making `cli-copilot` and `cli-claude-code` available for research iterations and rejecting settings their CLIs do not support. Phase 018 wired `cli-codex` as its only new executor and reserved the two new CLIs in the config enum while rejecting them at load time. The YAML workflow keeps ownership of state, convergence, lifecycle and the reducer, and this release ships as a symmetric pair with `deep-review` v1.6.0.0.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.9.0.0.md:25:- **Cross-CLI delegation is documented as design intent.** Both `SKILL.md` files gain a Cross-CLI Delegation subsection under the Executor Selection Contract. Any CLI executor can shell out to another CLI from its iteration sandbox, while self-recursive invocation is forbidden and each individual CLI skill warns against it. Users handle authentication and environment propagation because each CLI uses its own credentials and the deep-loop workflow does not mediate them. Runtime enforcement is out of scope.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/behavior-benchmark/baselines/claude-baseline.md:19:research INIT fail closed (correct workflow behavior), so it is NOT used for
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.3.0.0.md:17:The split is intended to make the workflow easier to follow and easier to trust.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md:17:The goal is to make the workflow easier to follow and easier to trust.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md:26:- **Lifecycle-mode claims are corrected.** A post-release update retracts two modes that had no workflow behavior.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md:62:On 2026-04-11, a post-release correction clarified that only `resume` and `restart` had workflow behavior. `fork` (start a sibling lineage) and `completed-continue` (reopen a finished run) had none, and selecting either silently did the same thing as `resume`.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/three-signal-model.md:19:The three-signal model is the statistical core of deep-research convergence. It gives the workflow a reusable way to judge diminishing returns without relying on a single novelty threshold.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22:The auto workflow admits the exact reasons `composite_converged` and `all_questions_answered`. A successful pivot selects a new focus from persisted adjacent questions, contradiction or verification gaps, missing source classes, alternate evidence methods, and independent finding checks. The shared adapter runs exactly three native seats in one round, persists the transaction under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, restores the selected focus, and continues the loop.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/verify-yaml-script-paths.sh:2:# Verify that Node .cjs script paths referenced by deep-loop workflow YAMLs exist.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/verify-yaml-script-paths.sh:44:printf 'PASS checked %d script references across %d workflow YAMLs\n' "$checked" "${#YAML_FILES[@]}"
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.2.0.md:17:- **Deep-research advances to version `1.2.2.0`.** `SKILL.md` aligns to the canonical packet contract, and the `deep-research` command updates its research and review workflow contract to the new packet layout.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.2.0.md:18:- **Workflows use the new paths.** The `speckit_deep-research_*.yaml` workflows update their research and review init, iteration and synthesis paths.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/changelog/v1.2.2.0.md:21:- **Wrapper naming aligns to `/speckit:deep-research`.** The `.agents` command wrappers and the `spec_kit_research.md` workflow now use that name.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/anti-convergence-floor.md:25:The config template defines `antiConvergence.minIterations` with a default of `3` and `antiConvergence.convergenceMode` with a default of `default`. The auto workflow writes those values into the config record, validates older or malformed configs at read time, and clamps the effective floor to the hard `maxIterations` cap when needed.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/anti-convergence-floor.md:27:During convergence checking, a STOP candidate is blocked while the completed iteration count is below the effective floor. When the floor clears, the workflow emits `min_iterations_guard_pass`, keeping attribution separate from quality-guard events. `convergenceMode: "off"` disables convergence-driven STOP while leaving max iterations, pause, and other explicit halts active.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark.md:20:one of the five `behavior_benchmark` packages carried by the deep-loop workflow
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/stuck-detection.md:19:Stuck detection is the loop's way of noticing that research is circling. It prevents repeated low-value passes by moving the workflow into a recovery branch with a different angle.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/stuck-detection.md:25:The workflow computes `stuckCount` from the JSONL history. It increments the counter when an evidence iteration falls below the configured convergence threshold or self-reports `stuck`. `insight` resets the counter because a conceptual breakthrough still counts as progress, while `thought` is skipped because it is not evidence gathering.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/loop-wide-dry-run.md:25:`/deep:research` normalizes `--dry-run` into a boolean workflow input. When enabled, the confirm YAML keeps non-mutating setup and read work live, then emits terminal JSONL preview events instead of appending to the state log or touching persistent artifacts.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-cli-lineages-research.md:30:- Expected signals: `step_fanout_spawn` present in YAML with `skip_when`; `step_fanout_merge` present in `phase_synthesis` with `skip_when`; `--executor` docs list 2+ → `config.fanout` default policy; `fanout-run.vitest.ts` confirms pool isolation.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-cli-lineages-research.md:49:1. `bash: grep -n "step_fanout_spawn\|step_fanout_merge\|fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\|skip_when" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml | head -20`
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/quality-guards.md:25:The legal-stop bundle is explicit. After a stop nomination, the workflow checks that each key question has evidence-backed coverage, that research stayed aligned with the original question set, and that the answered set is not leaning on a single tentative source. A stop is legal only when both the convergence gate and these guard checks pass together.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/quality-guards.md:27:Guard failures are visible packet events, not quiet side effects. The workflow emits `guard_violation` lines for the specific issue and then persists a `blocked_stop` event with gate results, blocker names, recovery guidance, session identifier, and generation. The reducer uses those events to update next focus, blocked-stop history, and dashboard reporting for the next loop turn.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/graph-convergence.md:25:When iteration records carry `graphEvents`, the workflow calls the deep-loop graph convergence tool and writes a `graph_convergence` event into the JSONL log. The live graph signals include component count, isolated nodes, edge density, and answer coverage. Those signals become part of the legal-stop evaluation instead of living only in notes.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/graph-convergence.md:27:The reducer consumes the newest `graph_convergence` event and surfaces its verdict in the synchronized packet outputs. `findings-registry.json` stores graph score, decision, and blockers, and `deep-research-dashboard.md` renders those values for operators. If no graph events are present, the workflow omits graph checks and the reducer defaults those fields without breaking ordinary convergence.
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/graph-convergence.md:41:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | CLI script | Produces the graph convergence verdict that the workflow records and the reducer consumes. |
.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-native-sequential-research.md:3:description: "Validate that native fan-out (count:N for the native executor) dispatches N sequential agent: deep-research runs with per-lineage isolated artifact dirs via config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir."
